<title>FRANCE: Total nine-month sales rise.</title>
<headline>Total nine-month sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover				     125,414    vs  100,590</p>
<p>    -- upstream				    8,321    vs    7,039</p>
<p>    -- downstream				 98,299    vs   76,803</p>
<p>    -- chemicals				  18,424    vs   16,515</p>
<p>    -- holding					 370    vs	233</p>
<p>NOTE -- Total SA said in a statement that the year end operating environment features a relatively strong Brent crude price and higher, albeit volatile, refining margins.</p>
<p>On the other hand, European marketing margins have been under pressure from higher refined product prices. It said hydrocarbons production is maintained at the first half 1996 level, a strong increase versus the 1995 level.</p>
</text>
